{% macro render(params = {}) %}
  {% import "atoms/svg/ui-components-loop.njk" as UiComponentsLoop %}
  {%- set sectionId = params.id | default("process") -%}
  {%- set copy = params.copy | default({}) -%}
  {%- set heading = copy.heading | default("Process") -%}
  {%- set body = copy.body | default("") -%}
  {%- set headingId = params.headingId | default(sectionId) -%}
  {#- Opt-in: renders the looping UI-components scene hooks. Pair with the
      `ui-components-loop` process variant in SECTION_OVERRIDES to activate. -#}
  {%- set uiComponents = params.uiComponents | default(false) -%}

  {%- set title = {
    "base": "col-span-full basis-full text-neutral-100 font-display font-light text-5xl",
    "md": "text-6xl",
    "lg": "text-7xl"
  } -%}

  <section id="{{ sectionId }}"
           class="h-dvh my-12 text-neutral-100 relative z-10 col-span-full grid grid-cols-subgrid p-0 overflow-hidden"
           aria-labelledby="{{ headingId }}"
           data-scroll-section>
    <header data-process-el="header"
            class="gap-2 px-8 py-12 z-10 flex flex-row items-center">
      <h2 id="{{ headingId }}"
          data-process-el="heading"
          class="{{ title | classes }}">{{ heading }}</h2>
    </header>
    {% if body %}
      <p data-process-el="body" class="col-span-full px-8">{{ body }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if uiComponents %}
      {# Looping index-and-dwell UI-components scene — first of two Process
         visuals across all breakpoints (see SECTION_OVERRIDES["process"]); the
         blockframes grid renders further down, after the first paragraph.
         Decorative; the JS scene
         (molecules/process-motion/ui-components-loop.js) binds via
         data-process-el, never a class. #}
      {# Height-driven, aspect-correct box: the svg's preserveAspectRatio
         "xMidYMid meet" fits-and-contains the full CHROME viewBox (no vertical
         crop). Width follows the ~square viewBox aspect (svg h-full w-auto,
         wrapper w-fit), so there are no letterbox side bands. Nudge the height. #}
      <div class="col-span-full mx-auto w-fit max-w-full h-48"
           data-process-el="uicomponents-stage"
           aria-hidden="true">
        {{ UiComponentsLoop.render({"classes": "h-full w-auto max-w-full text-neutral-100"}) }}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    <p>Most of the projects I work on as an experience designer are the product of a cross-functional team of stakeholders, managers, designers, and developers. Each team member has their own priorities and perspectives. My role is to ensure that everyone has the insight and direction they need to make informed decisions about how to serve the needs of users.</p>
    {#
      Blockframes 12x3 grid (WxH) — the second live Process visual, placed
      after the first paragraph. Built alongside the ui-components-loop scene
      by the composed `ui-components-loop` variant in
      PROCESS_VARIANT_FACTORIES. The grid fills the wrapper 1:1 (w-full
      h-full, 12 columns x 3 rows, no gap) so every cell is naturally 1/12
      the wrapper's width and sits flush against its neighbors — no
      oversizing, offset, or scale transform needed. All 36 cells are
      invisible placeholders cycling the 17 library block names; they are
      filled at runtime by choreography/molecules/process-motion/
      blockframes-grid.js via [data-blockframe-block] and revealed by
      blockframes.js's grid-stagger timeline.
    #}
    {%- set blockNames = [
      "Basic",
      "Features",
      "Blog",
      "Landing",
      "Chart",
      "Contact",
      "Cart",
      "Calendar",
      "Login",
      "Video",
      "Project",
      "Article",
      "Map",
      "List",
      "Text",
      "Main",
      "Feed"
    ] -%}
    <div class="relative w-full h-48 col-span-full overflow-hidden mx-auto"
         data-process-el="blockframes"
         aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="grid h-full w-full grid-cols-12 grid-rows-3"
           data-process-el="blockframes-grid">
        {%- for i in range(0, 36) %}
          {# No hiding class needed: cells are empty until JS fills them,
             and the reveal timeline holds them at autoAlpha 0 until then. #}
          <div data-blockframe-block="{{ blockNames[i % 17] }}"></div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>This is more than just figuring out where to place a button or how to word a call-to-action. It's about understanding the business goals, the user needs, and the technical constraints, and then finding the best way to balance them.</p>
  </section>
{% endmacro %}
